          <div class="rounded-xl border border-border/60 bg-card/30 p-7">
            <p class="cww-gold-deep-text font-body text-xs tracking-[0.14em] uppercase mb-5">Not ordinarily appropriate</p>
            <ul class="space-y-3">
              {notAppropriate.map((item) => (
                <li class="flex gap-3 items-start">
                  <svg class="w-4 h-4 shrink-0 mt-1 text-muted-foreground/60" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M6 18L18 6M6 6l12 12" /></svg>
                  <span class="font-body text-base text-foreground/78 leading-relaxed">{item}</span>
                </li>
              ))}
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="border-l-2 border-primary/40 pl-6 space-y-5">
          <p class="font-body text-lg text-foreground/78 leading-relaxed max-w-[62ch]">In a small team, can that reporting really be anonymous? Honestly, no. Even apparently anonymous thematic reporting can identify people, and it should be treated as identifying. In those settings reporting stays especially minimal.</p>
          <p class="font-body text-lg text-foreground/78 leading-relaxed max-w-[62ch]">Management can encourage or formally refer someone to seek support, and performance expectations remain a management responsibility throughout. Where any feedback is expected as part of that, the employee should know exactly what may be shared before counselling begins.</p>
          <p class="font-body text-lg text-foreground/78 leading-relaxed max-w-[62ch]">Mediation, formal assessment, or a report supporting an employment decision is a materially different professional role, and may need to be held separately from an employee’s private counselling. It is worth raising early rather than at the point it becomes urgent.</p>
        </div>

        <p class="font-body text-base text-foreground/72 leading-relaxed max-w-[65ch] mt-10 pt-8 border-t border-border/60">
          Wellbeing support can contribute to better functioning at work. It should never become a covert tool for surveillance or discipline. <a href="/privacy/" class="cww-inline-link">Read the privacy policy</a>, or the <a href="/scope/" class="cww-inline-link">full scope and ethics</a>.
        </p>
